    "body": "## \ud83d\uddd2\ufe0f Description\n\n### What\n- Refined bot event classification in `resolve_event_policy` to distinguish between autonomous partner bots authoring PRs (`cline-cloud[bot]`, `google-labs-jules[bot]`) and internal/suppressed loop bots (`hannibal-hub-agents[bot]`, `coderabbitai[bot]`).\n- Added an immediate short-circuit in `execute_agent_event` when `policy.mode == Mode.IGNORE`, returning empty actions and preventing session allocation or conversational dispatch fallthrough.\n\n### Why\n- On PR #389, Cline opened a PR with author login `cline-cloud[bot]`. The recently added unified policy layer blanket-matched all `*.endswith(\"[bot]\")` logins into `Mode.IGNORE`.\n- Because `policy.mode` was not `Mode.FORMAL_AUDIT`, `execute_agent_event` selected the `conversational_runner` and fell through to `_post_conversational_reply`, posting the raw audit JSON directly into the PR comments thread as an unformatted issue comment instead of a structured GitHub Pull Request Review (`pr.create_review`).\n- Furthermore, events resolved to `Mode.IGNORE` should never invoke runners or dispatch conversational comments.\n\n### How\n1. In `src/webhook_agent/core/policy.py`:\n   - Imported `is_hannibal_bot_login` from `bot_identity.py` to suppress internal app loop events.\n   - Defined `PARTNER_BOT_LOGINS` (`google-labs-jules[bot]`, `cline-cloud[bot]`, etc.) and `SUPPRESSED_BOT_LOGINS` (`coderabbitai[bot]`, `github-actions[bot]`).\n   - Allowed PR lifecycle events (`canonical in FORMAL_REVIEW_EVENTS`) from partner bots to resolve to `Mode.FORMAL_AUDIT`, ensuring zero-bypass code reviews.\n   - Preserved review-intent comment triggers for partner bots while suppressing unprompted bot comment chatter.\n2. In `src/webhook_agent/core/execution.py`:\n   - Added an immediate early-return guard checking `if policy.mode == Mode.IGNORE: return []` right after policy resolution.\n3. In `tests/unit/core/test_execution.py`:\n   - Added unit test coverage for partner bot PR audits, review-intent comments, unprompted bot comment suppression, own-bot loop suppression, and the `execute_agent_event` short-circuit guard.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83e\uddea Testing\n\n### Test Commands\n```bash\n./scripts/ruff-all.sh\nuv run pytest tests/unit/core/test_execution.py\nuv run pytest --tb=short -q\n```\n\n### Test Results\n- `./scripts/ruff-all.sh`: Linting, formatting, and MyPy passed with 0 issues.\n- `tests/unit/core/test_execution.py`: 40/40 passed.\n- Full suite (`pytest --tb=short -q`): 869 passed, 1 skipped, 36 deselected in 76s.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udce6 Configuration Impact\n\n- [x] No environment variables changed\n- [x] No dependencies added\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd12 Security Checklist\n\n- [x] No secrets or credentials hardcoded\n- [x] HMAC signature verification logic unchanged\n- [x] Zero-bypass review policy preserved for external autonomous bots\n- [x] Bot self-loop prevention maintained\n\n---\n\n## \ud83d\udd17 Related\n\n- Discovered on #389\n",
